--TEST--
A `return;` under a declaration that is not `void` is refused where it is written, at every door a body arrives through — `rule:types/declaration`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// A non-`void` declaration promises a value at every exit, and a bare
// `return;` is the exit carrying none. What makes one legal is the declared
// type alone, so the constructor below keeps its own: it declares no return
// type at all, and `E0248` is the other half of that pair.
class Sum {
    public int $total;

    public function constructor(int $total) {
        $this->total = $total;
        return;
    }

    public int $doubled {
        get {
            return;
        }
    }

    public static function of(int $n): int {
        return;
    }
}

var $f = fn (int $x): int => { return; };
echo $f(1), "\n";
--EXPECT--

--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0822]: `Sum::$doubled::get` declares `int` but this `return` hands back nothing
%A
error[E0822]: `of` declares `int` but this `return` hands back nothing
%A
error[E0822]: the anonymous function declares `int` but this `return` hands back nothing
%A
error: aborting due to 3 errors
To read what a code means and how to fix it, run `nvs agent show <code>`.
